// Creation date
Date: 2025-09-13

Description: The Signal Processing Toolbox provides a collection of functions for
 signal analysis, transformation, and synthesis in Scilab. It is designed to
 help users perform common signal processing tasks such as:
 - Signal generation (sine, square, triangular, etc.)
 - Frequency-domain transformations (FFT, DFT, etc.)
 - Digital filtering (FIR, IIR, Butterworth, Chebyshev, etc.)
 - Basic spectral analysis and convolution tools.

 This toolbox is useful for engineers, researchers, and students working in
 communication systems, audio processing, biomedical signal analysis, and
 general signal transformations.


 Example usage:
 --> t = 0:0.01:1;
 --> x = sin(2*%pi*10*t);
 --> y = fft1(x);
 disp(abs(y), "FFT Magnitude:")
